Collecting a repetition into an `; @array` — the working implementation.

Design-stage, not applied. Two repositories, in this order:

  tabnas/bnf   ts/src/compiler.ts, go/emit.go, go/ir.go (+ their tests)
  tabnas/abnf  ts/doc/guide.md, ts/test/value-annotation.test.js,
               test/spec/alignment-abnf-ast.tsv

Measured against @tabnas/parser 0.9.5, @tabnas/bnf 0.1.14,
@tabnas/abnf 0.4.11.

STATUS. Complete and green in TypeScript: bnf 117/117, abnf 391 unit
tests, and eleven new cross-runtime rows. The Go half emits a
byte-identical GrammarSpec — verified by diffing both CLIs' JSON — but
returns the wrong VALUES at parse time, for an engine reason described
in §6 of array-repetition.md. Do not apply the bnf half until that is
fixed: it would leave Go dropping elements, which is worse than the
run-as-text it replaces.

